diff --git a/docs/timer.md b/docs/timer.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..937f495
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/timer.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Question timer
+
+Quiz settings include "Timer minutes" and "Timer seconds" (integers, 0 by default). The time per question is `minutes * 60 + seconds`. 0 and 0 means no timer: the question stays open until the moderator clicks "Finish".
+
+The timer is a setting of this Quizzy. It is not part of the export or import format. An imported quiz starts with no timer.
+
+## During a game
+
+Start (and each Next) snapshots the quiz's current duration onto the game (`question_timer_seconds`). Editing settings does not change a question that is already open, and reloading does not restart the countdown. The next question that opens picks up the latest setting.
+
+The deadline is `question_opened_ms + duration`. That is the same moment the question opens for answers, including the 120ms open lead in production. The displayed countdown is capped at the full duration, so the lead does not show an extra second. Format is M:SS (`1:30`, `0:05`), minutes unpadded, seconds always two digits.
+
+Only the moderator big screen shows the countdown (`.stage-timer`). Player phones do not.
+
+At 0:00 the open question closes by itself, the same as clicking "Finish": counts and "Correct" on the big screen, `Correct!` / `Wrong!` / `No answer` on phones. The moderator can still click "Finish" earlier. "Next" / "End quiz" stay manual.
+
+Expiry is checked on moderator and player requests (including polls), so it does not depend on a background job. The big-screen countdown itself ticks in the browser from the server deadline, using `X-Quizzy-Now` to stay on the server clock.
